# Sample store environment. NAMES ONLY -- never commit values.
# Set these in the store's Vercel project.

# REQUIRED. Shared secret for GET /api/store/state. Without it the endpoint
# returns 503 and reads nothing. Set the SAME value wherever the edge-case
# finder runs (your shell for the CLI and MCP server, the console's Vercel
# project for hosted runs) so it can read the store's state.
REHEARSAL_STORE_TOKEN=

# REQUIRED. The same Supabase project the receiver uses, but a different table
# (store_order_events). Without BOTH, the webhook endpoint returns 503 rather
# than accepting a delivery it would then drop.
# The key is sent on the apikey header only: sb_secret_ keys are not JWTs.
SUPABASE_URL=
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=

# REQUIRED. This endpoint is public, so the PayPal signature is the only thing
# that distinguishes PayPal from anyone else. Without these the store CANNOT
# verify, so it records every event as refused and fulfills nothing, and answers
# 503 so PayPal retries once it is configured.
PAYPAL_SELLER_CLIENT_ID=
PAYPAL_SELLER_CLIENT_SECRET=

# REQUIRED: ONE OF THESE TWO. The store needs to know which PayPal webhook is
# its own, and never takes that from the request's Host (audit 2026-10-25 L4).
# With neither set it verifies nothing and answers 503 to every delivery.
#
# The store's own origin, exactly https://host with no path. The store asks
# PayPal which webhook points at origin + /api/paypal/webhook.
REHEARSAL_STORE_ORIGIN=
# Or pin the webhook id, which skips that lookup on every cold instance.
REHEARSAL_STORE_WEBHOOK_ID=
